"JORI Engine" is this project's own reference implementation. The name, and
the lowercase "jori" token derived from it, are recorded as implementation and
format identifiers in:

  - package metadata (the distribution's summary);
  - the "conversion" record of a generated manifest.json, which an exported
    bundle copies into the frontmatter of its derived/ and source/ documents;
  - the schema identifiers jori-corpus/v1, jori-manifest/v3, jori-manifest/v5,
    jori-manifest/v6, and jori-projection/v1; and
  - the "Canonical JORI corpus" resource title carried in an exported bundle's
    derived/ and source/ documents.

These are identifiers in a wire format and in generated output. No trademark
or brand right is asserted in the name.

This distribution contains no third-party source code.

Documentation in this repository quotes and paraphrases e-Gov-published
content; see docs/licensing-and-attribution.md for that material's
attribution.
